KZ2 patch 6054: VSync option (ENHANCEMENT) and a Present that never blocks the frame thread.

From two Killzone 3 port patches (the Killzone 3 PC port "Project Helghast", same author, MIT), adapted to KZ2's tree:
- KZ3 patch 2103 (Project Helghast port/patches/2103-vsync-option-tearing-present.patch): the swap chain gets
  DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_ALLOW_TEARING when IDXGIFactory5 reports DXGI_FEATURE_PRESENT_ALLOW_TEARING (ResizeBuffers repeats
  the flags); vsync off = Present(0, DXGI_PRESENT_ALLOW_TEARING) in a window or borderless, Present(0, 0) in exclusive
  fullscreen; on = Present(1, 0), the old call and the default. LD_PRESENT_INTERVAL (patch 2007, diagnostic) still wins.
  rsx_display_mode.h gets the pure parts (rsx_dm_parse_vsync, rsx_dm_present_args; tools/runtime/test_display_mode.c).
  KZ2 differs: the setting is a port row of the game's own Display page (port/kz2/kz2_port_rows.h "vsync", display.ini
  [display] vsync = on|off, KZ2_VSYNC=on|off for one run) applied through rsx_live_draw_set_vsync, instead of KZ3's
  Options-page injection and rsx_null_backend.c message.
- KZ3 patch 2127 (Project Helghast port/patches/2127-present-never-blocks-frame-thread.patch): a frame-latency waitable
  object (maximum latency 2); a Present whose slot is not free within LD_PRESENT_WAIT_MS (default 16 = one vblank) is
  skipped, so the frame thread (vblank ticks, FIFO drain, flips: port/kz2/main.cpp frame_clock) runs on. KZ3 found a
  window the compositor does not show blocking each Present for ~1 s (fps 1, then a vblank burst). LD_PRESENT_WAIT_MS=-1
  = the old blocking Present. "[present] skipped" lines count skips.
Both present sites (the game's flip and the movie present) go through ld_present_swap; patch 6040's Present-failure
recovery (ld_dm_present_result) wraps it as before. Why KZ2 takes them (Fable frame plan 2026-11-03, step 1c, rank 7):
KZ2 presented with Present(1, 0) on a 2-buffer FLIP_DISCARD chain, no tearing, no waitable object, so on a real 60 Hz
display a full flip queue can hold the walker for up to a vblank per frame (ASSUMPTION: not measured on a real display;
under Xvfb the present flush is 0.03-0.05 ms per flip). Under Xvfb nothing changes with vsync on.

